Quaker granola and -

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.360
what? Thank you - Cascadian 

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:05.700
granola, when I look at the nutritional profile and
they're both

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:09.340
the same, although, in fact,

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.800
to be, to be perfectly

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.870
fair, I believe that Quaker had less sugar,

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:17.480
but Cascadian Farms had a little more fiber.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.470
So they were, but they were roughly equivalent
and

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:23.120
neither of them tasted any good by the
way.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:28.620
So I don't want to stand, stand here and
say unequivocally

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:30.830
organic food is good, 'cause it's not.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:35.100
So the organic food has potential and some organic
food is good,

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:37.810
but if you're choosing between

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:43.100
an organic hamburger and a non-organic apple,
the apple is almost always going to be the

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.730
better choice. And I, so I wind up

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:51.180
sounding like a scoundrel who's against organic
foods, which I'm not but I don't think it's the most

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:53.780
important thing. I wouldn't go so far as to
saying

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:57.000
it's a red herring like I think salt is a red herring,

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:57.900
but I think

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:59.820
the reason that

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:03.490
organic food has become so popular, and this
goes back to this question, is that the food

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:09.540
marketers saw an opportunity for tremendous
profits in a very specialized upscale market

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.290
and they seize it. And they did not say

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:15.750
this spirit of organic food, as we know,

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:21.150
is whole foods. The spirit is rebuilding the earth.
The spirit is providing people with great nutrition.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:25.180
They said here's an opportunity to make money
by growing organic food.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:30.760
So they set up great farms in Chile that didn't
use pesticides and herbicides, which is very nice,

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:34.450
but you're still flying bad grapes from Chile
up to here

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.180
and now you're calling them organic. Grapes is not the best

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.540
example because

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.470
in a way there's nothing wrong with grapes,

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:47.470
but Cascadian Farms granola is a really good example 'cause it's crap.

